---
description: MR/PR titles must follow conventional-commit format
alwaysApply: true
---

Every merge request and pull request title must use Conventional Commits:
`<type>(<scope>): <subject>`. Same types, scope rules, and subject style as
the `conventional-commits` skill (imperative, ≤50 chars, no trailing
period). Type from the change content, not the ticket name.

Apply when creating or updating an MR/PR (`gh pr create` / `gh pr edit`,
`glab mr create` / `glab mr update`, GitHub/GitLab MCP equivalents). Never
ship a free-form, sentence-case, or ticket-only title (`Fix bug`,
`Update docs`, `ABC-123`). Optional scope when it adds signal; `!` or a
`BREAKING CHANGE:` footer for breaking changes.

Draft vs ready does not relax this — the title is conventional from the
first pushable open.
